## Why This Is Asked

This problem tests interval DP and both memoization and tabulation approaches. It asks for precise state definitions, correct recurrence when ends match, and careful base cases. It also probes understanding of time/space trade-offs for cubic-time DP.

## Key Concepts

- DP on substrings
- Memoization vs tabulation
- Interval DP with matching ends

## Code Example

```javascript
function minPalRemoval(s){
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=n-1;i>=0;i--){
    dp[i][i] = 1;
    for(let j=i+1;j<n;j++){
      dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i+1][j];
      for(let k=i+1;k<=j;k++){
        if(s[i] === s[k]){
          const left = (k-1 >= i+1) ? dp[i+1][k-1] : 0;
          const right = (k+1 <= j) ? dp[k+1][j] : 0;
          dp[i][j] = Math.min(dp[i][j], left + right);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return n ? dp[0][n-1] : 0;
}
```

